@startuml Agents
title Agents — Direct PROV-O Reuse and Physical Machines

skinparam groupInheritance 2
skinparam ArrowColor DarkRed
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide circle

class "prov:Agent" as Agent #LightYellow;line:DarkRed;text:DarkRed
class "prov:Person\n<size:11><color:gray><i>Menselijke Agent</i></color></size>" as Person #LightYellow;line:DarkRed;text:DarkRed
class "prov:Organization\n<size:11><color:gray><i>Organisation</i></color></size>" as Organization #LightYellow;line:DarkRed;text:DarkRed
class "prov:SoftwareAgent\n<size:11><color:gray><i>Running software actor</i></color></size>" as SoftwareAgent #LightYellow;line:DarkRed;text:DarkRed
class "ebwsm:Machine\n<size:11><color:gray><i>Physical software-controlled actor</i></color></size>" as Machine #LightYellow;line:DarkRed;text:DarkRed {
 +runsSoftwareAgent :
}

Agent <|-- Person #line:DarkRed;text:DarkRed
Agent <|-- Organization #line:DarkRed;text:DarkRed
Agent <|-- SoftwareAgent #line:DarkRed;text:DarkRed
Agent <|-- Machine #line:DarkRed;text:DarkRed
Machine::runsSoftwareAgent -left-> SoftwareAgent #line:DarkRed;text:DarkRed

note bottom of Machine
  Examples: an automated payment terminal or autonomous robot.
  Software execution and physical actor have separate identities.
  The software-agent link has no minimum or maximum count.
  Agent/Machine membership does not grant permission or a mandate.
end note

legend top left
  prov: classes and their existing hierarchy come from the pinned import.
  Machine and runsSoftwareAgent are WEBUILD extension terms (ebwsm:).
  No separate WEBUILD Agent class or Dublin Core Agent alignment.
  Sibling classes are not declared disjoint or exhaustive.
endlegend
@enduml
